Triage bug {{.key}}: "{{.title}}".

SEVERITY: {{.severity}}

READ: Bug report at {{.file_path}}

ASSESS this bug:
(1) Reproduce or confirm: can this be reproduced? Is the description sufficient?
(2) Classify severity: critical (data loss, security, complete feature broken), high (major feature impaired, no workaround), medium (feature impaired, workaround exists), low (minor, cosmetic)
(3) Check for duplicates: shark bug list --json | look for similar titles/descriptions
(4) Validate it is indeed a bug vs expected behavior

ROUTE:
- Clear bug with sufficient info → shark status set {{.key}} triaged --note='TRIAGE: severity={severity}, description={reason}' then update severity if needed: shark bug update {{.key}} --severity={corrected_severity}
- Duplicate of another bug → shark bug note {{.key}} 'DUPLICATE of {other_key}: {reason}' then shark status set {{.key}} duplicate
- Not a real bug / expected behavior → shark bug note {{.key}} 'WONT_FIX: {reason}' then shark status set {{.key}} wont_fix
- Insufficient info to reproduce → shark bug note {{.key}} 'NEEDS_INFO: {what is missing}' (leave in reported for human follow-up)
